## Auto-imported modules available in every Mezze file.
use std::abilities::sized
use std::abilities::numeric
use std::abilities::compare
use std::abilities::logic
use std::abilities::convert
use std::abilities::default
use std::abilities::inspect
## Tryable ability: `it.try {}` unwraps a `Result`/`Option` in a `perform`
## scope, short-circuiting on the failure case via `<Exception>`. Handle the
## `<Exception>` row with `perform ExceptionToResult` (from
## `std::effects::exception`) to fold it back into a `Result`.
use std::abilities::tryable
## Arbitrary is DERIVED for every record and variant, the way Eq is — so a module
## that never mentions sampling still has instances generated for the types it
## declares, and each of those calls `Arbitrary.arbitrary` on its components. Both
## the ability and its hand-written primitive impls therefore have to be in scope
## everywhere, which is what this line is for: `Eq` needs no such thing only because
## `==` on a primitive lowers to an inline comparison node instead of consulting an
## impl, and generation has no equivalent. A newtype still opts in by writing its own.
use std::abilities::arbitrary
use std::int
use std::float
use std::nat
use std::frac
use std::bool
use std::str
use std::char
use std::option
use std::result
use std::collections::seq
use std::collections::list
use std::collections::map
use std::collections::set
use std::collections::deque
use std::collections::sorted_map
use std::collections::sorted_set
use std::collections::nonemptylist
use std::collections::bytes
